{
 "name": "Skylight",
 "notes": "The hour and the minute very tall in a lens-shaped window between two shutters. Behind them is the sky, whose middle changes with the hour: deep at night, lighter towards midday, indigo again in the evening. The shutters' inner edges catch its light and their shadow falls on the figures; the seconds are cut out of the top of the last figure, where all ten figures have ink, so the sky shows through them. The weekday and the date in the top shutter; weather, charge, heart and steps in the bottom one. Every picture is drawn by make_case.py.",
